module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.MorphismToProjUniversal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedSectionRing.NatPowerSystem

/-!
# The Veronese restriction of a graded map `ψ : A^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L)`

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a graded ring, `Y` a scheme, `L` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module and
`ψ : A^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L)` a graded ring map, carried by its homogeneous components
`𝒜 (n d) →+ Γ(L ^⊗ n, ⊤)` as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.VeroneseSections`.
For a weight `k` the source restricts `ψ` to the smaller Veronese subring `A^{(kd)}`, whose
degree-`m` piece is `𝒜 (m k d)`, and reads the result as a graded map into
`Γ_*(Y, L^{⊗ k})`, whose degree-`m` piece is `Γ((L^{⊗ k}) ^⊗ m, ⊤)`. The two sides are related
by the comparison `(L^{⊗ k}) ^⊗ m ≅ L ^⊗ (km)`.

This file builds that comparison, proves it multiplicative, and assembles the restricted graded
map together with its generation condition.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjVeroneseRestrict.powVeroneseIso`: the comparison
  `(L^{⊗ k}) ^⊗ m ≅ L ^⊗ (km)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjVeroneseRestrict.veroneseRestrict`: **the Veronese restriction
  of `ψ` at a weight `k`**, a graded map `A^{(kd)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L^{⊗ k})`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjVeroneseRestrict.mulSections_powVeroneseIso`: **the comparison is
  multiplicative** for `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections`, the product of
  global sections of tensor powers.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjVeroneseRestrict.iSup_nonvanishingOpen_veroneseRestrict`:
  **`L^{⊗ k}` is generated by the degree-`kd` values of the restricted map**, in the geometric
  form Section 27.12 uses the generation condition — their nonvanishing opens cover `Y`. The
  covering family is the one of `ψ` itself: the value of the restriction at `f ^ k` is the
  `k`-th power `ψ(f)^k`, which is nonvanishing wherever `ψ(f)` is.

## Implementation notes

Both families of candidate tensor powers of `L^{⊗ k}` are `Stacks.Monoidal.PowerSystem`s on the
same generator: the iterated powers of `L^{⊗ k}` are `Stacks.GradedSections.natPowerSystem` of
`L ^⊗ k`, and the Veronese presentation `m ↦ L ^⊗ (km)` is
`Stacks.Monoidal.PowerSystem.veronese` of the iterated powers of `L`. So `powVeroneseIso` is the
generic comparison `Stacks.Monoidal.PowerSystem.compare` of two power systems along the identity
of their generators, and its multiplicativity is the generic
`Stacks.Monoidal.PowerSystem.compare_sectionMul`; no induction on the degree is run here.

What carries that over to honest sections is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections_globalSection`, which identifies the
product of sections with `Stacks.GradedSections.mul`, together with
`Stacks.GradedSections.mul_eq_sectionMul`, which identifies `Stacks.GradedSections.mul` with the
product of global sections of a power system. The only transport that remains is on the
exponent: the product of a section of `L ^⊗ (kp)` with one of `L ^⊗ (kq)` has exponent
`kp + kq`, while the degree-`(p + q)` piece of `Γ_*(Y, L^{⊗ k})` has exponent `k(p + q)`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NB)
